# UC-014 · GraphQL adapter

> Partial of `docs/use-cases/UC-014-cancel-order/`. Owner: `graphql-api-architect`.
> Inherits the canonical names from `00-caso-de-uso.md`, the input ports and the exceptions from
> `10-dominio.md`, and — this case's trigger being `inbound REST and GraphQL adapters` — the REST
> operations over the same ports from `30-rest.md`. Doesn't redecide them. Contains no code. Form
> references in `.claude/skills/graphql-api-architect/templates/`.
> Rules applied, never reproduced: `@.claude/rules/api-graphql.md`.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Parent spec | `00-caso-de-uso.md` — Trigger: `inbound REST and GraphQL adapters` |
| Domain partial | `10-dominio.md` |
| GraphQL package | `adapter.in.graphql` (blueprint `packages.map`) |
| Schema file | `src/main/resources/graphql/order.graphqls` |
| Spring for GraphQL line | the one the Boot parent of `pom.xml` manages; the starter is the Initializr's `graphql`, version empty |
| Divergences from other partials | none |

## 1 · Operations

One row per root field. Each calls an input port — the same one `30-rest.md` names for the same
operation, when there is one.

| Root field | Kind | Input port | Returns | REST counterpart |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `Query.order(id)` | query | `FindOrderQuery.find` | `Order` (nullable) | `GET /api/v1/orders/{orderId}` |
| `Query.myOrders(first, after)` | query | `ListMyOrdersQuery.list` | `OrderConnection!` | `GET /api/v1/orders` |
| `Mutation.cancelOrder(input)` | mutation | `CancelOrderUseCase.handle`, then `FindOrderQuery.find` | `CancelOrderPayload!` | `POST /api/v1/orders/{orderId}/cancellation` |

## 2 · Schema

Types, fields and nullability, as written in the schema file. Every type has an adapter record of the
same name, mapped by hand from the port's read model.

| Type | Field | Type | Nullable — why | Source |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `Order` | `id`, `status`, `placedAt`, `total` | `ID!`, `OrderStatus!`, `String!` (ISO-8601 UTC), `Money!` | no | `OrderView` |
| `Order` | `lines` | `[OrderLine!]!` | no — empty, never null | batch, § 5 |
| `Order` | `customer` | `Customer!` | no — an order always has one | batch, § 5 |
| `Customer` | `taxId` | `String` | yes — denied without `SUPPORT` (§ 8, `32-seguranca.md`) | `CustomerView`, its own guarded mapping |
| `Money` | `amount`, `currency` | `String!`, `String!` | no | decimal as text |

## 3 · Inputs and payloads

| Mutation | Input fields and shape validation | Payload | `userErrors` codes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `cancelOrder` | `orderId: ID!` `@NotNull`; `reason: String` `@Size(max = 500)` | `CancelOrderPayload { order, userErrors }` | `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` (field `["input","orderId"]`), `ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED`, `ORDER_ALREADY_CANCELLED` |

A partial update: none in this case — no input distinguishes "absent" from "null".

## 4 · Pagination

| Connection | Directions | Order (unique key last) | Default / max page | Cursor carries |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `myOrders` | forward (`first`, `after`) | `placedAt` desc, `id` desc | project setup § 6: 20 / 100; above 100 is `BAD_REQUEST` `PAGE_SIZE_OUT_OF_RANGE` | `placedAt`, `id` → `ListMyOrdersQuery.OrderCursor` |

## 5 · Batch loads

Every child field that costs I/O. The batch port is a **requirement**: `10-dominio.md` did not declare
it, and consolidation carries it to the domain block with this partial as who asked.

| Field | Batch port (requirement) | Key | Missing key answers | Max batch |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `Order.lines` | `OrderLinesQuery.linesOf(Set<UUID>) → Map<UUID, List<OrderLineView>>` | `Order.id` | empty list | project setup § 6 |
| `Order.customer` | `CustomersQuery.byIds(Set<UUID>) → Map<UUID, CustomerView>` | `Order.customerId` | — an order always has a customer | project setup § 6 |

## 6 · Project setup

First GraphQL case of the project: decided here, written once by the executor, inherited by every
later case. A later partial writes `inherited from UC-014` and changes a value only with a reason and
an impact row.

| Limit | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Max depth | 8 | the deepest legitimate document is 4 (`order.lines.unitPrice.amount`); twice that leaves room for new types |
| Max complexity | 2000 | a full page of 100 orders with lines and customer costs about 1 000 |
| Request timeout | 5 s | the slowest port is measured at 900 ms p99 |
| Default / max page | 20 / 100 | the same contract as REST (`@.claude/rules/api-rest.md` § Pagination) |
| Max batch | 100 | equal to the max page: one page, one `IN` list |
| Introspection | off; on in `dev` | `@.claude/rules/api-graphql.md` § Demand limits |
| GraphiQL | `dev` only | same |
| CORS | `POST`, origins from `GRAPHQL_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`, none by default | asked: the web client is served from another origin |
| Schema inspection | fails the startup | same |
| Endpoint in the filter chain | `POST /graphql` authenticated | `32-seguranca.md` § 1 |

## 7 · Error map

| Situation | Where it lands | Classification | `errorCode` |
|---|---|---|---|
| Order missing or not the caller's — query | top-level, `order` null | `NOT_FOUND` | `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` |
| Order missing or not the caller's — mutation | `userErrors` | — | `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` |
| Already shipped / already cancelled | `userErrors` | — | `ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED` / `ORDER_ALREADY_CANCELLED` |
| `reason` above 500 characters | top-level | `BAD_REQUEST` | `INVALID_INPUT` |
| `first` above 100 | top-level | `BAD_REQUEST` | `PAGE_SIZE_OUT_OF_RANGE` |
| `taxId` without `SUPPORT` | top-level, field null | `FORBIDDEN` | — |
| Anything else | top-level | `INTERNAL_ERROR` | — |

Project-wide pieces: `GraphQlExceptionResolver`, `GraphQlConfig`, `GraphQlLimits` — NEW.

## 8 · Personal data

Every output field walked through `@.claude/rules/logging.md` § Masking candidates.

| Field | Form | Receiver and reason |
|---|---|---|
| `Customer.name` | full value | the customer seeing their own order, and support — the screen shows it |
| `Customer.taxId` | full value, `SUPPORT` only | support verifies identity on a cancellation dispute — recorded by the user on 2026-10-13; guarded on the field |

## 9 · Requirements to other partials

| To | Requirement |
|---|---|
| `10-dominio.md` | the batch ports of § 5 |
| `20-persistencia.md` | one statement per batch port (`IN` over the keys, bounded by § 6's max batch); an index serving `customer_id, placed_at desc, id desc` for § 4's order |
| `32-seguranca.md` | one row per root field of § 1 and one for `Customer.taxId` |

## 10 · Contract test cases

| Level | Case |
|---|---|
| GraphQL slice | `order` mapped field by field; `order` not found → `NOT_FOUND` + `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, field null; `cancelOrder` refused → `userErrors[0].code`, `order` null; `reason` above 500 → `BAD_REQUEST`, port never called; a page of two orders → one `linesOf` and one `byIds` call with both keys; an edge's cursor sent back as `after` → the port receives that order's `OrderCursor`; `first: 101` → `BAD_REQUEST` |
| HTTP, real chain | anonymous → 401 from the chain; `taxId` without `SUPPORT` → null + `FORBIDDEN`, the rest intact; with `SUPPORT` → the value; depth above the limit → refused, no port called; introspection → refused |
| Schema | the served schema against `src/test/graphql/schema.snapshot.graphqls` — created by this case |

